                    <p>
{!Contact.FirstName},<br /><br />

Thank you for your interest in the graduate programs within the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Arizona State University. I hope you will take a closer look at the exciting things going on in our department by visiting our  <a href=http://chemistry.asu.edu/Graduate/Prospective/index.asp>prospective student</a> page
to learn more about the department and our graduate programs.<br /><br />

The department offers PhD degrees in both chemistry and biochemistry, and all admitted students are fully funded, including the cost of tuition, health insurance and a competitive stipend..</a><br /><br />

Applications are currently being accepted for study beginning fall 2015. The application deadline is Jan. 15, 2015. We will not be admitting students for spring 2015.<br /><br />

Applying is a two-part process consisting of a general graduate application through the graduate admissions office and a supplemental application to the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry. More detailed information about the application process is available on our <a href=http://chemistry.asu.edu/graduate/applicantInfo.asp>prospective student - how to apply</a> page as well as our <a href=http://chemistry.asu.edu/graduate/FAQ.asp>FAQ</a> page.<br /><br />
We are a growing program that is <a href=http://chemistry.asu.edu/graduate/facultyResearch.asp>conducting cutting edge, interdisciplinary research</a> to solve societal problems at the molecular level, and I encourage you to check out the research being conducted by our faculty. I hope you will consider joining us.<br /><br />
If you have questions about the application process or graduate programs that are not included on our website, please email me and I will be happy to assist you.<br /><br />
Good luck in your pursuit of graduate studies.<br /><br />

David Nutt<br />
Graduate Programs Coordinator <br />
Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry<br />
<a href="mailto:david.nutt@asu.edu?Subject=Request%20For%20Information"target="_top">David Nutt@asu.edu</a><br />
